-- title:
--   Nondegeneracy in the operator variable of the a₁-pairing
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let $T$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphism of the space $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ of cusp forms of weight $2$ for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_0(N)$. Assume first that $T$ lies in the $\mathbb{C}$-linear span, inside $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$, of the underlying set of [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), that is, of the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra generated by the operators `heckeTLin 2` attached to the primes $\ell$ not dividing $N$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to the primes $q$ dividing $N$ (the excluded set of primes being empty, so that all these generators occur). Assume second that for every cusp form $f \in S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ the first coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $Tf$ at width $1$ vanishes, i.e. $a_1(Tf) = 0$, where $a_n(g)$ denotes the $n$-th coefficient of `UpperHalfPlane.qExpansion 1 g`. The conclusion is that $T = 0$ as an endomorphism of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$.
--
--   This is the operator half of the nondegeneracy of the pairing $\mathbb{T}_{\mathbb{C}} \times S_2(\Gamma_0(N)) \to \mathbb{C}$, $(T,f) \mapsto a_1(Tf)$, between the complexified Hecke algebra of level $N$ and weight $2$ cusp forms; the membership hypothesis is essential, since a general endomorphism of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ killing all $a_1(Tf)$ need not vanish. It is used in the construction of Frobenius-type algebra homomorphisms out of the Hecke algebra and in the Hecke-equivariant comparison of the rational Tate module and the period lattice of a modular curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_eq_zero_of_mem_span_heckeAlgebra_of_forall_qCoeff_one_eq_zero.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_FLTPrelim_Modularity

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.eq_zero_of_mem_span_heckeAlgebra_of_forall_qCoeff_one_eq_zero (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (T : Module.End ℂ (CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2))
    (hT : T ∈ Submodule.span ℂ (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (∅ : Set ℕ) : Set (Module.End ℂ (CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2))))
    (h : ∀ f : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2, ModularFormClass.qCoeff (T f) 1 = 0) :
    T = 0 := by sorry
